# Type definitions are cloned by tools\setup.ps1, not authored here.
types/

# Per-computer runtime state written in game, not source.
#
# `tools\link-world.ps1` junctions a test world's computer folder straight at
# `src/`, so every dotfile the OS writes at runtime lands in the working tree.
# All of them are listed, not only the ones seen so far: a turtle that gets as
# far as mining writes six of these within a minute, and a `git status` full of
# them is how a real change gets committed with somebody's saved position in it.
.door
.pulse
.update
.settings
.node
.nav
.log
.location
.site
.mine
.fleet
.gps
.expedition
.rare
.resources
.quarry
.hollow
.swarm
.fuel_hunt
# Every config write lands as `<name>.tmp` first; a crash can leave one behind.
*.tmp
*.bak-*
